	doi = {10.1177/20438869231216995},
	abstract = {This teaching case examines the challenges of designing a digital solution to address complex sustainability problems. The case follows the vice president for innovation of a mid-sized European digital agency involved in a project dedicated to designing a digital application that connects climate-conscious investors, banks, and homeowners in need of loans for green house renovations. In this case, students need to navigate stakeholders’ conflicting needs and consider broader aspects of environmental, social, and economic sustainability in the design of digital applications. At the same time, this digital solution should seek to promote stakeholders’ dignity. © Association for Information Technology Trust 2023.},
